export const HOST_AGREEMENT_SECTIONS_A = "3. COMPANY OBLIGATIONS\n\nThe Company shall perform the following services (the \u201cServices\u201d) in accordance with all applicable laws, regulations, and car-sharing platform policies:\n\n- Create and maintain listings for the Vehicle.\n\n- Provide optimized pricing strategies designed to maximize Vehicle bookings.\n\n- Provide guest and trip management services.\n\n- Take pre-trip and post-trip photos and complete check-in and check-out requirements.\n\n- Wash the Vehicle before each trip.\n\n- Handle all communication between Owner, guests, and third parties, as applicable.\n\n- Use the Vehicle for marketing and advertising purposes.\n\n- Coordinate damage and insurance claims.\n\n- Coordinate basic vehicle maintenance and repairs.\n\n- Provide parking for the Vehicle.\n\n- Provide reports to the Vehicle Owner.\n\n4. OWNER OBLIGATIONS\n\nTo ensure the Company can deliver the Services, Owner agrees to provide the following in accordance with all applicable laws, regulations, and car-sharing platform policies:\n\n- Provide the Vehicle in good working condition and meeting the Company listing requirements.\n\n- Arrange transportation of the Vehicle to and from the Company\u2019s business location.\n\n- Maintain full coverage insurance for the Vehicle at all times.\n\n- Remit monthly applicable Vehicle financing or lease payments, if applicable.\n\n- Remit payment and keep current annual Vehicle registration, including tax and title fees.\n\n- Deliver Vehicle registration and stickers to the Company within one week of receipt.\n\n- Provide payment or reimbursement to the Company for any and all costs associated with Vehicle maintenance, servicing, or repairs on a monthly basis unless deducted by the Company from Owner\u2019s earnings.";
export const HOST_AGREEMENT_SECTIONS_B = "6. TICKETS AND FEES\n\nThe Company will manage and process any fines or toll charges incurred during the reservation period, to the extent possible. The Company reserves the right to recover these costs from the guests linked to the booking at the time of the violations. Owners are required to promptly report any tickets or toll charges by uploading corresponding documentation into the the Company system. Tickets and toll charges must be submitted at least one week prior to the due date. Failure to do so may result in the Company not covering fines accrued thereafter. The Company shall not be held responsible for any tickets and tolls incurred while the Vehicle is in Owner\u2019s possession.\n\nThe following fees may be deducted from the Owner\u2019s balance:\n\n- Parking fee: $75 per month. The Company collects the parking fee monthly to ensure the car is safely parked during off-trip periods. If the Vehicle is removed from the Company at the Owner\u2019s request (unlisted) or becomes inoperable/requires repairs, the Owner must retrieve the Vehicle within 72 hours of submitting the unlisting request or receiving notice that the Vehicle requires repairs or is inoperable. If the Vehicle is not picked up within this 72-hour period, a parking fee of $35 per day will apply until retrieved.\n\n- Service fee: $35 per service. Applied when vehicle maintenance services are provided, including oil and filter changes, tire replacement, battery replacement, and glass replacement. The cost of these services is not included in the service fee.\n\n- Repair fee: $95 per service. Applies for vehicle repair services, including engine, transmission, suspension, electrical, bodywork, and rim repairs. For repairs over $500, a repair fee will be charged; for repairs under $500, a service fee will apply instead.\n\n- Delivery fee: $75 (one way). Applies when the Owner requests vehicle delivery between their location and the the Company lot, or to a dealership, repair shop, or other designated place. Delivery covers up to 15 miles from the Company; each additional mile costs $5. No delivery fee applies for repairs within 2 miles of the the Company location.\n\n- Claim fee: $95 per claim. Charged when the Company processes a claim. Covers administrative costs associated with managing and processing the claim.\n\n- GPS installation and removal fee: $150. Applies if a GPS tracking device was installed by the Company and the Owner withdraws the Vehicle within 30 days from the start of the management period.\n\n- Failure to return GPS device fee: $300. Applies if the Owner does not return the GPS device within the agreed timeframe after withdrawal from the Company service.\n\n- Photo/video production fee: $150. Applies if photo or video production services were provided for marketing or listing purposes and the Owner withdraws the Vehicle within 30 days from the start of the management period.\n\n- Convenience fee: $35. Applied when the Company provides services to the Owner that were not previously agreed upon or described in this Agreement.\n\n- Expired registration and tags fee: $100 plus the full amount of the impacted trip. Applied for failure to register the Vehicle within the required timeframe or failure to provide current registration and stickers in a timely manner. Earnings for the impacted trip will not be added to gross rental revenue.\n\n- Trip cancellation fee: $50 per each canceled reservation. Applied if the Owner retrieves the Vehicle while it has upcoming reservations scheduled within the next 30 days.\n\n- Penalty for guest reservation interference: $250 plus the full amount of the impacted trip. Any deliberate action aimed at obstructing a guest reservation period (including remotely disabling the engine or unauthorized retrieval during a reservation) will result in this penalty. If an Owner retrieves the Vehicle without prior notification and the Company has an upcoming reservation within the next 24 hours, the Company may penalize the Owner. Earnings for the impacted trip will not be added to gross rental revenue.\n\n7. PARKING\n\nThe Company provides secured parking between reservations. However, the Company does not assume responsibility for the Vehicle or any valuables therein while parked on the the Company parking lot. The Company declares itself not responsible for fire, theft, damage, or loss of the Vehicle. The Company and its insurer(s) are not responsible for any personal property, including any aftermarket installations that are taken from the Vehicle or damaged during a reservation period. Owner should remove all personal property before making the Vehicle available for a reservation.\n\n8. INSURANCE\n\nAll trips are covered by state-minimum liability insurance through a third-party insurer, with up to $110,000 in physical damage coverage. The Company does not provide insurance and disclaims any responsibility for coverage. Insurance may be provided by a third-party insurer or the renter\u2019s own policy.\n\nVehicle owners must maintain active full coverage insurance at all times, including liability, collision, and comprehensive coverage. In the event of a claim, the platform or its insurer may require proof of the Owner\u2019s active full coverage. Failure to maintain such coverage may result in claim denial or refusal to cover any related damages, losses, or liabilities.\n\n9. MAINTENANCE\n\n- The Vehicle must be delivered to the Company by Owner fully serviced and ready for rentals.\n\n- The Owner must provide accurate information regarding the most recent service date.\n\n- the Company will manage routine maintenance tasks, including oil changes, tire replacement, and other standard procedures, to keep the Vehicle in optimal condition for rentals. Costs of routine maintenance will be deducted from the Owner\u2019s balance along with a service fee. The Company will provide transparent billing and documentation for all maintenance expenses.\n\n- Owner hereby authorizes the Company to undertake any necessary maintenance or repairs on the Vehicle, provided that the total cost does not exceed Three Hundred Dollars ($300), without prior notice or consent from the Owner.\n\n- Ensuring the Vehicle remains in a serviced condition is the responsibility of the Owner.\n\n10. REPAIRS\n\n- The Owner is responsible for ensuring that the Vehicle is delivered to the Company in good working condition, free from any major mechanical issues or defects.\n\n- It is the Owner\u2019s responsibility to maintain the Vehicle in good working condition.\n\n- In the event of any necessary repairs, the Company will coordinate and manage the repair process on behalf of the Owner. Owner authorizes the Company to perform repairs at the Company partner facilities. Repairs not exceeding $300 will be undertaken without advance confirmation. Repairs exceeding $300 will be carried out with the Owner\u2019s consent.\n\n- Repairs costing over Five Hundred Dollars ($500) shall be paid by the Owner, unless the Owner\u2019s the Company account balance covers the cost of the repair.\n\n- If the repair estimate exceeds One Thousand Dollars ($1,000), the Owner must retrieve the Vehicle within 72 hours after receiving confirmation from the Company. In such cases, the repair must be arranged and completed by the Owner independently.\n\n- Costs associated with repairs deemed necessary for safe operation will be deducted from the Owner\u2019s balance (along with the Repair fee), unless covered by warranty or insurance.\n\n- the Company will provide timely communication and updates regarding any repairs needed, as well as transparent documentation of all repair expenses.\n\n- Owner reserves the right to perform repairs independently, provided they comply with all relevant regulations and safety standards.\n\n11. CLAIMS\n\nAll trips are covered by state-minimum liability insurance through a third-party insurer, with up to $110,000 in physical damage coverage. In the event of a claim for physical damage, a deductible shall apply in accordance with the protection plan selected under the Earnings and Payments section.\n\n- Owner authorizes the Company to handle the entire claim-resolution process and perform repairs at certified service centers and BAR-licensed body shops at the Company\u2019s discretion. Owner agrees to cooperate fully in the resolution of any claims and provide additional data upon request. Failure to cooperate may result in cancellation of claim payments.\n\n- All documents and invoices related to claims can be provided to the Owner upon written request via email to Talent@DimesOnly.World.\n\n- If the Vehicle is declared a total loss, the Company will inform the Owner within 72 hours of receiving this notification.\n\n- Owner bears full responsibility for any claims and damages to the Vehicle, as well as damages to third parties, if the Vehicle was inoperable, did not have valid registration, or lacked an insurance policy at the time of the incident, or if insurance coverage is denied for those reasons.\n\n- the Company shall not be held responsible for any claims, Vehicle damages, or damages to third parties if the Owner refuses to cooperate or violates this Agreement.\n\n- the Company shall not be held responsible for any pre-existing damage.\n\n- the Company shall not be held responsible for any damages or claims that occurred while the Vehicle was in the Owner\u2019s possession.\n\nIf a third-party insurance provider or any car-sharing platform denies payment for a claim for any reason, the Company shall not be liable for payment of damages to the Owner, and the Owner shall seek payment from their insurance provider or the party at fault.\n\n12. UNCOVERED DAMAGES AND MILEAGE\n\nOwners acknowledge that normal wear and tear is expected due to rental use of the Vehicle. There is no reimbursement for interior and exterior wear and tear. Natural wear-and-tear-related breakdowns and breakdowns not associated with improper vehicle operation are not covered by the Company and are not repaired at the company\u2019s expense.\n\nExterior wear and tear is any dings, dents, cracks, or scratches to the Vehicle\u2019s exterior body that are three inches (or 7.5 centimeters) in diameter or less. It includes, but is not limited to, rims, wheels, hubcaps, any painted or textured area of the body, and moldings. It does not include cracked or chipped glass caused by rocks or other debris.\n\nThe Company is not responsible for the following aspects of vehicle maintenance and operation: headlight fogging, tires, battery, brake pads, shocks and struts, belts, hoses, and spark plugs.\n\nNormal wear and tear includes:\n\n- Vehicle paint, body, and bumper wear: scratches and bumper wear as a depression or contouring on a single panel 3 inches or less in diameter.\n\n- Tire wear: reduced tire tread and/or scuffs no longer than 3 inches in length on the tire\u2019s rim.\n\n- Windshield and windows: existing window cracks and scratches are especially susceptible to additional wear from continued use. This additional deterioration is normal wear and tear.\n\n- Interior trim, carpet, upholstery, and controls: minor scuffs to interior surfaces measuring less than 3 inches in diameter. The Company is not responsible for dents or scratches to truck beds arising from intended use, or for weathered or worn convertible-top upholstery from normal exposure.\n\n- Mechanical wear: all vehicle mechanical systems (electrical, suspension, engine, brakes, and transmission) experience wear over the course of the Vehicle\u2019s life. Owners are responsible for performing routine maintenance checks and keeping the Vehicle in working order.\n\nOwner consents to sharing the Vehicle for car-sharing purposes with unlimited mileage. The Company shall not be held responsible for any decrease in the Vehicle\u2019s value due to changes in vehicle mileage.\n\n13. VEHICLE RETURN\n\nMinimum Placement Term. The minimum duration for placing the Vehicle in the Company service is 30 days. After this initial period, Owner may request return of the Vehicle for any duration, provided there are no existing reservations during those dates. Owner understands and agrees that all upcoming booked trips must be completed first. There should be no upcoming trips scheduled for the Vehicle within the next 30 days. For each canceled trip, the Owner will be subject to a Trip Cancellation Fee. In the event of an unconfirmed retrieval resulting in cancellation of a reservation within 24 hours, a Penalty for Guest Reservation Interference may be applied.\n\nIf a guest wishes to extend a currently booked trip that would overlap with the period the Owner wishes to use the Vehicle, the Owner shall forgo such use and allow the guest\u2019s booked trip to be extended, but not exceeding 14 days.\n\nOwner-Requested Return Date. Owners may designate a date for return of the Vehicle. However, if the car is returned from a trip and insurance-covered damage is discovered, the Company reserves the right to retain the Vehicle until the claims process and repairs are completed.\n\nReturn Procedure. Owners must schedule an appointment with the Company in advance to retrieve the Vehicle. On the scheduled day, the Vehicle will undergo an inspection. If the Vehicle does not pass inspection and requires repair of damages covered by insurance, the Owner agrees to allow the Company to rectify those damages and subsequently retrieve the Vehicle. Upon completion of repairs, the Owner inspects the Vehicle and signs the Termination Agreement, thereby officially closing the contract.\n\nBy signing this document, the Vehicle Owner guarantees that the Vehicle has a clean title.";
